    {
      "id": "script-capability-smoke-instructions",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Smoke Procedure",
      "position": { "x": -420, "y": 60 },
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 380,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "ports": [
        { "id": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "any", "angle": 210 },
        { "id": "top", "label": "top", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "value", "angle": 270 }
      ],
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Smoke Procedure\n\n1. Confirm the import bridge adds two entries to Elements: **Collection Surface** and **Collection Window Controller**.\n2. Create each entry once. Do not copy configuration from another graph.\n3. Open the Controller Editor, set page size to `1`, and return to its Summary firing surface.\n4. Click **Apply Size**, then **Run**. One fixture card should appear.\n5. Click **Next** and **Previous** on the Controller. The visible fixture card should change and return.\n6. Set page size to `2`, apply it, and confirm both fixture cards appear.\n7. Open Controller Detail and confirm source, singleton multiplicity, requirements, effects, grants, and mutation policy are visible.\n8. Save and reload. The two authored kit nodes should persist; projected fixture portals must not.\n\n**Pass:** one export bridge transports an authored Collection Surface plus a fully class-backed, executable Script node. The Controller presents its own controls and only transient member portals are created at runtime.",
        "visibilityRole": "browser"
      }
    },
